From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:59:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tdeioslave/sftp: report the creation time as a creation time

stat() and listDir() appended the server's creation time under
UDS_MODIFICATION_TIME, after the real modification time. The copy job
reads the entry in order and keeps the last value, so every file
copied over sftp got the creation time as its modification time.

OpenSSH speaks SFTP version 3, which has no creation time, so libssh
leaves createtime at zero and every copy was dated 1 January 1970.
Reproduced against stock OpenSSH:

    kfmclient copy sftp://user@127.0.0.1:2299/tmp/x/hello.txt file:///tmp/got/
    stat -c %y /tmp/got/hello.txt      # 1970-01-01 01:00:00 CET

Report it as UDS_CREATION_TIME, which the copy job already reads, and
only when the server sent one (SSH_FILEXFER_ATTR_CREATETIME). An absent
creation time is better left out than reported as 1970.

The line came in with the backported slave in fd94618b.
---
 tdeioslave/sftp/tdeio_sftp.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tdeioslave/sftp/tdeio_sftp.cpp b/tdeioslave/sftp/tdeio_sftp.cpp
index 3e88b8e6..52fdd9d5 100644
--- a/tdeioslave/sftp/tdeio_sftp.cpp
+++ b/tdeioslave/sftp/tdeio_sftp.cpp
@@ -797,9 +797,12 @@ notype:
     atom.m_long = sb->mtime;
     entry.append(atom);
 
-    atom.m_uds = UDS_MODIFICATION_TIME;
-    atom.m_long = sb->createtime;
-    entry.append(atom);
+    // SFTP v3, which OpenSSH speaks, carries no creation time.
+    if (sb->flags & SSH_FILEXFER_ATTR_CREATETIME) {
+      atom.m_uds = UDS_CREATION_TIME;
+      atom.m_long = sb->createtime;
+      entry.append(atom);
+    }
   }
 
   sftp_attributes_free(sb);
@@ -2042,9 +2045,12 @@ notype:
       atom.m_long = dirent->mtime;
       entry.append(atom);
 
-      atom.m_uds = UDS_MODIFICATION_TIME;
-      atom.m_long = dirent->createtime;
-      entry.append(atom);
+      // SFTP v3, which OpenSSH speaks, carries no creation time.
+      if (dirent->flags & SSH_FILEXFER_ATTR_CREATETIME) {
+        atom.m_uds = UDS_CREATION_TIME;
+        atom.m_long = dirent->createtime;
+        entry.append(atom);
+      }
     }
 
     sftp_attributes_free(dirent);
